When installing _libmavsdk-dev_2.12.5_ubuntu22.04_amd64.deb_ I can't build the ftp_client example due to the following compile errors:

`home/alex/MAVSDK/examples/ftp_client/ftp_client.cpp: In function ‘mavsdk::Ftp::Result remove_directory(mavsdk::Ftp&, const string&, bool)’:
/home/alex/MAVSDK/examples/ftp_client/ftp_client.cpp:73:62: error: ‘ListDirectoryData’ is not a member of ‘mavsdk::Ftp’`

A quick investigation shows that by installing the deb the following header file is included:
_/usr/include/mavsdk/plugins/ftp/ftp.h_

The relevant lines of code are as follows in this file:
```
    /**
     * @brief Destructor (internal use only).
     */
    ~Ftp() override;

    /**
     * @brief Progress data type for file transfer.
     */
    struct ProgressData {
        uint32_t bytes_transferred{}; /**< @brief The number of bytes already transferred. */
        uint32_t total_bytes{}; /**< @brief The total bytes to transfer. */
    };
```

When building MAVSDK from source the examples work as the relevant lines of code are as follows in this file:
```
    /**
     * @brief Destructor (internal use only).
     */
    ~Ftp() override;

    /**
     * @brief
     */
    struct ListDirectoryData {
        std::vector<std::string> dirs{}; /**< @brief The found directories. */
        std::vector<std::string> files{}; /**< @brief The found files. */
    };
```

I have created a sender/receiver pair to exchange custom mavlink messages over SiK Radio.

ideally, I would like to minimize the amount of data being sent over the link and keep it as minimal as possible to conserve bandwidth.

Below is an example of each of the sender and receiver modules:

**Sender**

```
int main(argc, char* argv[])
{

    uint8_t drone_system_id = 2;
    uint8_t drone_component_id = 1;
    bool always_send_heartbeat = true;

    Mavsdk::Configuration config = Mavsdk::Configuration(drone_system_id, drone_component_id, always_send_heartbeat);
    Mavsdk mavsdk_drone{config};
    std::shared_ptr<mavsdk::System> peer_system_;

    //connect to the local serial radio and obtain the peer_system_
    auto mavlink_direct = MavlinkDirect{peer_system_};

    //define and load custom_xml

    //create an instance of the message
    MavlinkDirect::MavlinkMessage msg_name{};

    while(1){
        msg_name.fields_json = R"({...});
        auto result = mavlink_direct.send_message(msg_name);
    }

    std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(1000)); // 1Hz
    return 0;

}
```

**Receiver**

```
